  "limitations": [
    "The initial baseline auxiliary build overlapped an edit to the source, so its source read is ambiguous; a successful replay against the pinned original snapshot is the baseline used for comparison.",
    "The standalone target commands and zero exit statuses were observed in the active tool session; no independent machine-readable target status records were saved. Target logs and timing files are preserved; the focused checks and axiom reports do have per-command JSON status records.",
    "The parent authenticated 39 source pins from the prior cache; NativePellBootstrap and SignedPellResidue changed since that cache in addition to the two intentional Pell source edits. Earlier local prerequisites and external dependencies remained precompiled.",
    "ArithmeticConstructionBoundPell and ArithmeticConstructionAssembly directly import the auxiliary module and were not checked in this scope. ArithmeticPellFirstIndex is being rebuilt independently from the final half-index object.",
    "Object files and overlay links are excluded. Timing observations were made under concurrent load."
  ],
  "independent_review": "The original transport_equal and transport_opposite statements and proof bodies are byte-identical in the two modules. The change promotes the HalfIndex copies and removes the duplicated auxiliary copies and their now-unused helpers without changing prior public statements or imports. Original snapshots match the parent commit; the auxiliary replay snapshot matches the original. Two focused checks and all 29 old public axiom reports match byte-for-byte; both new public helpers have only the standard three axioms. No proof or API defect was found."
